sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant F as :Frontend
  participant G as :Gems
  participant DB as :Database
  participant LF as :Live Feed
  participant OF as :Frontend (another user)

  U->>F: open the dashboard
  F->>F: get the device's location (asks for permission if needed)
  F->>+G: GET /gem/newest (near the user's location, if granted)
  G->>+DB: find the newest gems
  DB-->>-G: gems, or an error
  G-->>-F: 200 [gems], or 500 "Get Gems failed."
  alt 200 gems
    F-->>U: the newest gems, with their photos
  else 500 database error
    F-->>U: "Couldn't load gems, try again"
  end

  alt location permission granted
    F-)LF: subscribe (user's location, radius)
    LF-)F: subscribed
    Note over OF,G: Another user adds a gem within the radius (Use Case 1)
    OF->>+G: POST /gem
    G->>+LF: publish the new gem
    LF-)F: gem.added
    LF-->>-G: done
    G-->>-OF: 201 gem
    F-)U: the new gem appears at the top of the list, without refreshing
    Note over F,LF: A rating in the area sends gem.updated the same way, and the Gem Score updates in place
    opt the live-feed connection is lost
      F-)U: "Live updates paused, reconnecting…"
      F-)LF: reconnect, then subscribe again
      LF-)F: subscribed
      F-)U: the message disappears, new gems appear again
    end
  else location permission denied
    F-)U: dialog: location is needed for live updates, the list shows the newest gems without live updates
  end
  Note over U,OF: If the server can't be reached, the Frontend shows "No connection, try again"
